  "body": "A [recent Twitter thread](https://twitter.com/amberweinberg/status/1265789076445290500) about whether a screenshotted table should be marked up as a table or a list concluded that it should be a table because it represents 2D data, but had to be a list because table rows can't be linkified. I feel like maybe this problem should be solved somehow so that authors aren't forced into poorer markup a11y in order to satisfy utility? Links as \"rows\" is a pretty common paradigm, so I imagine this same decision has been made many times for the same reasons.",
